hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1486","Musa bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, Abu Usama told us, Zaida bin Qadamah told me, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Hubaysh Al-Kala’i, h. Ali bin Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Zaida bin Qudamah narrated to us, Al-Sa’ib bin Hubaysh Al-Kala’i narrated to us, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha Al-Yamari said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: Where is your residence? I said: A village below Homs. Abu Darda said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There are not three people in a village, nor a Bedouin. So prayer will not be performed among them unless Satan takes control of them, so you have to pray in congregation, for the wolf only devours the stray animal.” Al-Masruqi said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the wolf takes the sting.”"
